  "how_these_were_read": "Each row was read straight out of the published text table, not out of the encoded asset, so it is an independent check of the encoder's axis order as well as of the accessor. sourceHeadingLine is the 1-based line of the section heading ('a) foF2 variability: lower decile, winter, R12 < 50' and its eight siblings per decile); the latitude rows follow two lines of chrome and run 90 degrees down to 0 in steps of 5, so sourceRowLine is heading + 3 + (90 - |latitude|) / 5. Within a row the first token is the latitude label and the remaining 24 are local-time hours 00 to 23, so the factor is token 2 + localTimeHours. month and r12 are the inputs that select that section: month picks the season for the hemisphere the latitude sign names (the southern rows here are the mirror test), and r12 sits inside the named range. Every latitude is a tabulated row and every hour a tabulated column, so a correct accessor reproduces the printed decimal exactly and no interpolation is exercised.",
